# Logitech G502 X LIGHTSPEED (046d:409f through its 046d:c547 receiver,
# 046d:c098 cabled) -> uaccess on its own hidraw node through the receiver,
# and on its HID++ interface, 02, on its cable.
#
# Not yet checked on this hardware. It is the G502 X PLUS without lighting,
# on the same receiver, so its rules are the X PLUS's hidraw rules in
# 70-g502x.rules, for the same reasons. Through the receiver the mouse's own
# node is matched by its HID device name: a property match would also take
# in the receiver's interfaces, which carry the input of everything paired to
# it. Pair nothing else to this mouse's receiver: going by the kernel's
# hid-logitech-dj.c, a keyboard paired after the mouse could have its
# keystrokes arrive on this node.
#
# Cabled, interface 02 is the vendor HID++ collection on the G502 X PLUS
# (00 the pointer, 01 a keyboard collection, read off that mouse on
# 2026-09-22); no published source gives this model's interfaces, so 02 is
# assumed. Interface 01 is not granted.
#
# No event node is granted: in host mode Gearbench reads the buttons it binds
# through HID++ on the hidraw nodes below, and outside host mode none.
KERNEL=="hidraw*", SUBSYSTEM=="hidraw", KERNELS=="0003:046D:409F.*", TAG+="uaccess"
KERNEL=="hidraw*", SUBSYSTEM=="hidraw", ENV{ID_VENDOR_ID}=="046d", ENV{ID_MODEL_ID}=="c098", ENV{ID_USB_INTERFACE_NUM}=="02", TAG+="uaccess"
